'''Takalak''' ('''Tagalaka''', '''Dagalag''') is a poorly attested, [[language death|extinct]] [[Australian Aboriginal languages|Australian Aboriginal language]] of [[Queensland]].

==Country==
The Tagalaka inhabited the area, estimated at {{convert|3,900|mi2|km2}}, in the middle of the Gilbert River, north nearly to the Einasleigh River, south to the Gregory Range, east to Georgetown and Forsayth and west to near Croydon.{{sfn|Tindale|1974|p=185}}

